          "source_excerpt": "Name of the Matter: | Confidential (Y/N):\nClient: SCOTCH\nMatter’s Value (specify currency) and/or other key numbers:\nMatter Status (closed in last year or ongoing?):\n\t\t\n\t\t\tMatter’s Context:\nSCOTCH engaged DeForest to review and restructure its corporate and labor framework following the introduction of Mexico's specialised services regime (REPSE). The matter required a multidisciplinary approach combining labor, corporate and regulatory expertise to ensure that the client's business model remained fully aligned with the country's evolving outsourcing framework.\n\t\t\n\t\tFirm’s role and main output:\nWorking jointly across its corporate and labor practices, DeForest carried out a comprehensive review of the client's corporate structure, specialised services model, bylaws and REPSE registration while simultaneously conducting an audit of more than eighty suppliers to determine the appropriate regulatory treatment of specialised services agreements.\n\nThe engagement demonstrates the firm's ability to advise clients on complex regulatory transformations where employment, corporate governance and commercial operations converge.\n\t\t\n\t\tLead Partner(s):\nJosé Alberto Díaz Méndez.\n\t\t\n\t\tOther team members:\nN/A\n\t\t\n\t\tOther firms advising on the matter and their role:\nN/A\n\t\t\n\t\tLinks to press coverage:\nN/A\nName of the Matter: | Confidential (Y/N):\nClient: Grupo Solana\nMatter’s Value (specify currency) and/or other key numbers:\nMatter Status (closed in last year or ongoing?):\n\t\t\n\t\t\tMatter’s Context:\nGrupo Solana, a diversified automotive and real estate group employing more than 1,200 people, retained DeForest to implement a complex employer substitution process affecting its workforce structure. The matter required careful coordination between labor and regulatory authorities to ensure business continuity while restructuring the group's employment platform.\n\t\t\n\t\tFirm’s role and main output:\nDeForest designed and executed the legal strategy necessary to reactivate the employer registration that had previously been cancelled, allowing the employer substitution process to proceed without disrupting the client's operations. The firm coordinated the labor transition while ensuring full compliance with applicable employment regulations and preserving workforce stability throughout the restructuring.\n\nThe engagement illustrates the firm's ability to support complex corporate reorganisations where labor law plays a critical role in enabling business transformation.\n\t\t\n\t\tLead Partner(s):\nJosé Alberto Díaz Méndez.\n\t\t\n\t\tOther team members:\nN/A\n\t\t\n\t\tOther firms advising on the matter and their role:\nN/A\n\t\t\n\t\tLinks to press coverage:\nN/A\nName of the Matter: | Confidential (Y/N):\nClient: Poliuretanos Summa Woodbridge (PSW)\nMatter’s Value (specify currency) and/or other key numbers:\nMatter Status (closed in last year or ongoing?):\n\t\t\n\t\t\tMatter’s Context:\nPSW engaged DeForest to design and implement a comprehensive restructuring affecting approximately eight companies operating across multiple Mexican states. The project required the separation of business functions, the redesign of the group's employment model and the creation of a specialised services platform aligned with Mexico's post-outsourcing regulatory framework.\n\t\t\n\t\tFirm’s role and main output:\nDeForest developed the legal strategy supporting the group's restructuring, including the creation of a specialised services entity, employer substitution processes, the redesign of corporate purposes and the implementation of a workforce transition affecting multiple operating companies. In parallel, the firm represents the client in social security litigation before the Federal Court of Administrative Justice challenging tax assessments relating to two manufacturing facilities, while continuing to advise on broader labor and social security governance matters.\n\nThe engagement reflects the firm's ability to coordinate multidisciplinary projects where labor law, corporate restructuring and social security litigation converge to support large-scale business transformation.\n\t\t\n\t\tLead Partner(s):\nJosé Alberto Díaz Méndez.\n\t\t\n\t\tOther team members:\nN/A\n\t\t\n\t\tOther firms advising on the matter and their role:\nN/A\n\t\t\n\t\tLinks to press coverage:\nN/A\n\n[Contenido adicional: footer1]\nLeaders League\n\t\t88, boulevard de la Villette\n\t\tParis – France, 75 019\n\n[Contenido adicional: footer2]\nLeaders League\n\t\t88, boulevard de la Villette\n\t\tParis – France, 75 019",
