          "userId": "90e761a0-451e-43a1-8099-5ee3c61de4e1",
          "summary": "Mextypsa, one of Mexico's leading engineering and infrastructure companies, relies on DeForest as its strategic labor counsel for projects where workforce governance is fundamental to successful execution. The firm's mandate extends beyond day-to-day employment advice, encompassing the design of labor structures capable of supporting large-scale infrastructure projects while preserving regulatory compliance and operational continuity throughout each project's lifecycle.\n\nOne of the most significant engagements involved the Guadalajara Metro Line 4 Project, a USD 552 million infrastructure development requiring a sophisticated labor framework to manage project-based recruitment, documentation, workforce administration and eventual demobilisation under intense public scrutiny. Simultaneously, DeForest represented the client in complex litigation arising from the Coahuila Wind Farm Project, where an adverse labor judgment threatened liabilities exceeding MXN 5.5 million.\n\nRather than treating these matters as isolated engagements, DeForest developed a comprehensive labor governance strategy combining preventive advisory with high-stakes dispute resolution. The team designed the contractual and compliance architecture supporting the Guadalajara Metro project, supervised workforce demobilisation to minimise post-project contingencies and successfully challenged the adverse labor judgment through constitutional proceedings, restoring the client's procedural rights and reopening the litigation.\n\nToday, the firm manages more than twenty labor disputes for Mextypsa representing aggregate exposure of approximately MXN 21.5 million. Through early negotiation strategies and disciplined litigation management, DeForest has consistently reduced financial exposure while protecting operational continuity across the client's infrastructure portfolio.",
