          "userId": "90e761a0-451e-43a1-8099-5ee3c61de4e1",
          "summary": "One of Mexico's most extraordinary labor disputes gave rise to this engagement. A former senior executive obtained a labor judgment exceeding MXN 2.162 billion, exposing Enerflex and indirectly PEMEX to unprecedented financial and governance risks. Against this exceptional backdrop, the employee retained DeForest to develop an alternative strategy capable of unlocking negotiations that had reached complete deadlock.\n\nRather than relying exclusively on litigation, DeForest designed a parallel mediation strategy running alongside the judicial proceedings. The firm established common valuation criteria, governance-based negotiation parameters and structured settlement mechanisms capable of facilitating constructive dialogue between parties that had previously been unwilling to negotiate.\n\nThe strategy ultimately generated a series of favourable settlement agreements that preserved the employee's legitimate interests while significantly reducing systemic exposure for Enerflex and preventing PEMEX from facing joint liability arising from one of the largest labor awards ever issued in Mexico. The matter remains ongoing, with DeForest continuing to coordinate negotiations alongside PEMEX's in-house legal team.\n\nThis engagement reflects the firm's ability to resolve disputes where legal complexity, commercial interests and public-sector exposure intersect at the highest level.",
